<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE suite SYSTEM "http://testng.org/testng-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Finance Smoke Suite — Account Group, AP Voucher, and AR Voucher have no functional
    dependency on each other, but they DO compete for the same shared SET1 UserPool (4
    configured UI users). Originally all three ran together in ONE <test> block
    (parallel="methods" thread-count="4") on the assumption that 4 threads == 4 users would
    keep the pool balanced — but AccountGroupLifecycle's own data/row instability (repeated
    "duplicate name" server rejections, tree-navigation mismatches) can leave a thread
    completely silent (no Selenium heartbeat) for the full pool.acquire.timeout.seconds
    window. Because ExecutionContext/DriverManager are thread-local and this engagement's
    deferred-logout + bounded-lease session reuse holds a user for many rows at a time, one
    unstable AccountGroupLifecycle holder was enough to starve every AP/AR Voucher row queued
    behind it (UserPoolAcquisitionTimeoutException cascade — see the incident RCA dated
    2026-07-08).

    Fix: two SEQUENTIAL <test> blocks instead of one shared block, with the suite itself
    staying parallel="none" (already the case). TestNG runs <test> blocks one after another
    under parallel="none", so AccountGroupLifecycle's block fully completes — and releases
    every user it held back to the pool — before the AP/AR Voucher block ever starts. This
    trades away the theoretical wall-clock overlap between the two blocks (which was already
    producing zero AP Voucher throughput once AccountGroupLifecycle stalled) for a hard
    guarantee that one class's instability can never starve the other's users again, with
    zero UserPool code changes required.

    data-provider-thread-count MUST be at suite level — TestNG ignores it on <test> — and
    caps concurrent DataProvider-driven invocations to 4 so the pool is never oversubscribed
    beyond the configured user count, in either block.

    Run: mvn clean test -DsuiteXmlFile=testng-smoke.xml
    Promote to regression later per the approved plan (Round 3, section 3.9).
-->
<suite name="Finance Smoke — Account Group + AP Voucher + AR Voucher" parallel="none" data-provider-thread-count="4">

    <listeners>
        <listener class-name="com.gsl.listeners.RetryAnnotationTransformer"/>
        <listener class-name="com.gsl.listeners.TestListener"/>
        <listener class-name="com.gsl.listeners.SuiteDataLoader"/>
        <listener class-name="com.gsl.listeners.AnnotationMethodInterceptor"/>
    </listeners>

    <!-- Runs to completion first, using the full 4-user pool by itself, however long it takes. -->
    <test name="Account Group Lifecycle" parallel="methods" thread-count="4">
        <classes>
            <class name="com.tests.Finance.Setup.AccountGroupLifecycle"/>
        </classes>
    </test>

    <!-- Starts only after the block above fully finishes and releases every user it held. -->
    <test name="AP AR Voucher" parallel="methods" thread-count="4">
        <classes>
            <class name="com.tests.Finance.Operations.Vouchers.CreateApVoucher"/>
            <class name="com.tests.Finance.Operations.Vouchers.CreateArVoucher"/>
        </classes>
    </test>

</suite>
